    "docs/audits/2026-10-03-frontend-design-system-audit.md (\"kill the 405 !important\").",
    "counts.print         - the print/PDF sheet. It runs after the screen rules and has to override",
    "                       selectors more specific than its own (`h1` vs `.prose-blog h1`), so the",
    "                       flag is the mechanism; removing any of these needs a print comparison.",
    "counts.reducedMotion - the prefers-reduced-motion block sits early in the file, so later",
    "                       animation declarations would win without the flag.",
    "counts.screen        - declared rules that beat an inline style (`style={{ \u2026 }}` on the same",
    "                       element). Utilities are in @layer utilities, so an unlayered selector",
    "                       already beats them and does not need the flag; the gate fails on any",
    "                       screen !important whose property no inline style in the app sets.",
    "The counts are a ratchet: they may fall, not rise. Run the script with --update after a pass",
    "that removes some, and say why in the commit."
